  "planning_notes": [
    "UNO board with verified wiring endpoints: D2 for the local toggle button input; D4/D5 for TM1637; D7 for DHT11. No other functional pins were provided and none are added.",
    "Serial receive is implemented via serial_command_input on the same physical Serial baud (9600) using ASCII tokens BOTH/HUMI/TEMP mapped to integer codes 1/2/3. Outgoing serial reporting uses serial_channels on the same baud and framing.",
    "Button model semantics: io model value is true when pressed. active_high is set to false and pullup is true to match typical wiring where pressed connects to GND; the runtime wiring layer should maintain model-pressed=true without additional inversion.",
    "DHT temperature/humidity share D7 and are published coherently with dht_valid; invalid_policy=hold_last_valid retains previous numeric values while dht_valid indicates frame validity.",
    "TM1637 invalid_policy=blank; initial display request is number 0 prior to serial/menu-driven updates. Control/report timing beyond sensor acquisition cadence is handled in the SysML model using elapsed_ms."
  ],
